
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Lily Flower</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f5fff5;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 15px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 12px #cccccc;
        }

        img {
            width: 100%;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        h1 {
            color: #e75480;
        }

        p {
            color: #444;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        button {
            background: #e75480;
            color: white;
            padding: 12px 25px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <div class="container">
        <h1>🌸 Lily Flower</h1>

        <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520763185298-1b434c919102?w=800"
            alt="Beautiful flowers"
        >

        <h2>About Lily</h2>

        <p>
            Lily is a beautiful flowering plant known for its
            elegant petals, attractive colors, and pleasant fragrance.
            It symbolizes purity, beauty, and love.
        </p>

        <button onclick="showMessage()">
            Learn More
        </button>
    </div>

    <script>
        function showMessage() {
            alert("Lily represents purity, beauty and elegance!");
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
